{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# rebar-debug must trace and record the defect's originating ticket before it closes a bug\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `rebar-debug` skill drives a bug to a proven, cited root cause, then throws\naway the provenance. Phase 1 ends with the mechanism, Phase 2 fixes it, and the\nticket closes without naming the ticket whose work introduced the defect. Defect\nescape rate cannot be measured when escaped defects are not mapped to an origin.\n\nrebar already has the machinery, so this is a skill gap, not a code gap:\n`caused_by` is a first-class relation (`graph/_links.py:CANONICAL_RELATIONS`);\n`rebar transition <bug> ... closed` accepts `--caused-by=<id>`\n(`_commands/transition.py:65,163`); the links feed the `bug_caused_by_fan_in`\nmetric (`metrics/bug_trends.py:255`) and the deterministic epic-close\n`caused_by` floor (`docs/plan-review-gate.md:1091`).\n\nAbsent an explicit `--caused-by`, a bug close silently falls back to blame\nauto-derivation (`metrics/blame.py:184-227`): it blames `<fixing-commit>~1`\nacross every path in the ticket's `file_impact` and takes a strict majority of\n**all lines in those files**. Two systematic failure modes follow. It attributes\nto whoever wrote most of the file rather than whoever wrote the defect. And\nbecause it only ever looks at the paths the *fix* touched, it cannot see the\ncommon case where the fix site is not the cause site — a producer change\nintroduces an obligation (new field, changed invariant, renamed API) and a\nconsumer is never updated, so the fix lands in consumer code whose lines may be\nyears old and correct-at-the-time. There, blame reliably charges the defect to\nthe consumer's old ticket instead of to the change that shipped the obligation\nwithout updating its consumers, which is exactly the escape worth counting.\n\nThe skill has strictly better evidence than that fallback and must supply it.\n\n## Plan\n\nAmend two skill files. No code, no behavior change.\n\n**A. `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` — defect attribution:**\n\n1. Add a required attribution step to Phase 1's exit gate (Stage 3), immediately\n   before the RCA writeback: find the introducing change by blaming the exact\n   lines the confirmed experiment implicated, walk through carrier commits\n   (reformat/rename/move), recover the ticket from that commit's\n   `rebar-ticket:` trailer or leading `<id>:` subject, and record it.\n2. Add an explicit \"the fix site is not the cause site\" sub-step covering unmet\n   obligations and missed consumer updates, with the date test as a cheap\n   detector (implicated lines predating the good-to-bad transition cannot have\n   caused it) and producer-side search (`git log -S<symbol>`) as the recovery.\n3. Route recording through the native surface: `--caused-by=<id>` paired with\n   the required `--class` on the bug close, or `rebar link <bug> <origin>\n   caused_by` when the link is wanted at the Phase 1 exit instead.\n4. Require attribution to meet the root cause's evidentiary standard and\n   inherit the fallback's fail-closed discipline, and enumerate four\n   resolutions: regression, unmet obligation, omission (attributed by\n   scope-of-work), and unattributable (record the searches, leave the link\n   unset).\n5. Scope attribution to the `defect` and `incomplete-implementation` paths; the\n   not-a-bug classifications have no defect to attribute.\n6. Gate the bug close on it in \"Reporting back\" and add a **Defect origin** line\n   to the report-back list.\n7. Wire the supporting hooks: add the link to the approval-gate own-tracker\n   carve-out so recording it needs no user approval; note attribution retention\n   on the fast path; point Stage 1's git-history bullet at the exit-gate step.\n8. State that `--caused-by` on the close is required whenever an origin is\n   known, even if the link was already recorded earlier via `rebar link`:\n   `_apply_caused_by` (`transition_close.py:198-201`) calls\n   `blame.derive_caused_by` unconditionally when `--caused-by` is empty and\n   never checks for an existing `caused_by` edge, so a bare close adds a second,\n   guessed edge beside the proven one.\n\n**B. Worktree bootstrap correctness in `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\nand `examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`:**\n\n9. Replace the bare `git worktree add <path> -b <branch> origin/main` bootstrap\n   with `make worktree name=<branch>`, noting that it provisions the worktree's\n   virtualenv where the bare form does not.\n10. Add one pointer in each skill: run every command with the worktree venv\n    first on `PATH` (`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" <cmd>`), because a fresh\n    worktree's venv is not on the ambient `PATH` and the pre-commit hook then\n    fails on a missing `ruff`/`mypy` even when the code is clean — see\n    `docs/local-dev-env.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `SKILL.md` contains an attribution step in Phase 1 Stage 3 that requires\n      identifying the originating ticket before the RCA writeback. Verified by\n      `grep -n 'Attribute the defect to its originating ticket' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning exactly one hit.\n- [ ] The step gives the literal close syntax including `--caused-by`. Verified\n      by `grep -c -- '--caused-by=<origin-id>' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning at least 1.\n- [ ] The fix-site-is-not-cause-site case is covered as its own numbered\n      sub-step. Verified by\n      `grep -n 'The fix site is not the cause site' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning exactly one hit.\n- [ ] The unattributable path is present and fails open to a recorded negative\n      result rather than a guess. Verified by\n      `grep -n 'Unattributable' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning at least one hit in the attribution section.\n- [ ] The bug close is gated on attribution in \"Reporting back\". Verified by\n      `grep -n 'Do not close the bug ticket until its origin is recorded' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning exactly one hit.\n- [ ] The own-tracker approval carve-out lists the `caused_by` link, so\n      recording it is pre-approved. Verified by reading the carve-out paragraph\n      and confirming the link appears in its enumerated writebacks.\n- [ ] The skill frontmatter gate still passes. Verified by\n      `python3 scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` exiting 0.\n- [ ] The close-time flag is stated as required even when a link already\n      exists. Verified by\n      `grep -n 'is not optional once you have an origin' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning exactly one hit.\n- [ ] Both skills bootstrap via `make worktree name=<branch>`. Verified by\n      `grep -c 'make worktree' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`\n      returning at least 1 for each file.\n- [ ] Both skills carry the venv-on-PATH pointer. Verified by\n      `grep -c 'docs/local-dev-env.md' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`\n      returning at least 1 for each file.\n- [ ] No source file changed. Verified by `git diff --name-only origin/main`\n      listing only the two skill files above.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis change is documentation-only (one Markdown skill file); it ships no Python\nand therefore adds no unit test. It is proven by the repository's own gates plus\nthe per-criterion greps above:\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py\ngit diff --name-only origin/main\nawk 'length>100 {print FILENAME\":\"FNR}' examples/agent-skills/rebar-*/SKILL.md\npython -m pytest tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py -q\nmake lint\n```\n\nExpected: frontmatter gate PASSes; the diff lists only the two skill files;\nthe line-length scan reports no lines over 100 characters that are not already\npresent on `origin/main`; `test_skill_shared_sync.py` passes (the shared\n`test-design.md` copies are untouched); `make lint` clean."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787182413156708001,"uuid":"e13bb7a7-e459-4409-add0-20f5d27d029d"}